$$
2b - 2c = \frac{1}{12} \Rightarrow b - c = \frac{1}{24}
$$

Now we have:

$$
a - b = \frac{1}{12} \tag{4}
$$
$$
b - c = \frac{1}{24} \tag{5}
$$

Add equations (4) and (5):

$$
a - c = \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{24} = \frac{3}{24} + \frac{1}{24} = \frac{1}{8}
$$

Now we can solve for $a, b, c$:

From equation (4):

$$
a = b + \frac{1}{12}
$$

From equation (5):

$$
b = c + \frac{1}{24}
$$

Substitute into equation (4):

$$
a = \left(c + \frac{1}{24}\right) + \frac{1}{12} = c + \frac{1}{24} + \frac{2}{24} = c + \frac{3}{24} = c + \frac{1}{8}
$$

So:

$$
a = c + \frac{1}{8}
$$

Now from $a + b + c = -\frac{13}{12}$:

$$
\left(c + \frac{1}{8}\right) + \left(c + \frac{1}{24}\right) + c = -\frac{13}{12}
